1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,712
What do you do when the bank's network never answers?

2
00:00:02,762 --> 00:00:05,664
Your parcel left, but tracking says nothing.

3
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:07,584
You do not post a second parcel.

4
00:00:07,634 --> 00:00:14,280
You check tracking, waiting a little longer each time, and before the post office closes, you go and ask in person.

5
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:20,376
An unknown charge is never declined, and never sent again, because the money may already have moved.

6
00:00:20,426 --> 00:00:28,632
A durable workflow remembers it, even across restarts, and asks the network only about this one charge, waiting longer each time.

7
00:00:28,682 --> 00:00:30,504
Found means paid.

8
00:00:30,554 --> 00:00:32,376
Not found means declined.

9
00:00:32,426 --> 00:00:36,144
Found after the buyer's page has closed, the money goes back.

10
00:00:36,194 --> 00:00:43,440
It stops before the day's deadline, and anything still unknown goes to manual review, where a person decides.

11
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:46,056
Next: how the shop hears about a payment.
